From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:45:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/UsbBusDxe: Bound BOS capability parsing

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0048, as it is]

UsbIsSSDevice() trusts device-reported NumDeviceCaps and capability
Length fields without bounding reads to the BOS buffer. Malformed values
can cause out-of-bounds reads and an exception during device enumeration.

Validate the BOS header and total length. Before reading each capability,
check that its header and declared length fit in the remaining bytes.
Reject malformed or truncated descriptors and recognize SuperSpeed only
after validating the complete capability list.

The unbounded parser was introduced by PR #12714:
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/pull/12714

Signed-off-by: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit bf25b6e4017b (merged on
2026-10-21, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: the parser of PR #12714 is in the base, and
UsbBuildDescTable() runs it for every device that reports USB 2.1 or
later. It walked NumDeviceCaps capabilities by their Length fields
without bounding them by the BOS descriptor it had read, so a device
with malformed values made the payload read past that buffer, by up to
about 64 KiB, while it enumerated the device at boot.

TEST=git am on the series: clean, at another offset (MrChromebox's
UsbDesc.c moves it), the same lines as upstream. No test with such a
device.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
index 106757ecb..be43bea7b 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbBusDxe/UsbDesc.c
@@ -355,22 +355,47 @@ UsbIsSSDevice (
   UINT8                       Index;
   UINT8                       NumCapDesc;
   EFI_USB_DEV_CAP_DESCRIPTOR  *DevCapDesc;
-
-  if ((BosDesc->DescriptorType != USB_DESC_TYPE_BOS) || (Len == 0)) {
+  UINTN                       Remaining;
+  UINTN                       CapLength;
+  BOOLEAN                     IsSsDevice;
+
+  if (  (BosDesc == NULL)
+     || (Len < sizeof (*BosDesc))
+     || (BosDesc->DescriptorType != USB_DESC_TYPE_BOS)
+     || (BosDesc->Length < sizeof (*BosDesc))
+     || (BosDesc->Length > Len)
+     || (BosDesc->TotalLength < BosDesc->Length)
+     || (BosDesc->TotalLength > Len))
+  {
     return FALSE;
   }
 
   NumCapDesc = BosDesc->NumDeviceCaps;
   NextCap    = (UINT8 *)BosDesc + BosDesc->Length;
+  Remaining  = BosDesc->TotalLength - BosDesc->Length;
+  IsSsDevice = FALSE;
+
+  for (Index = 0; Index < NumCapDesc; Index++) {
+    if (Remaining < OFFSET_OF (EFI_USB_DEV_CAP_DESCRIPTOR, CapData)) {
+      return FALSE;
+    }
 
-  for (Index = 0; Index < NumCapDesc; Index++, NextCap += DevCapDesc->Length) {
     DevCapDesc = (EFI_USB_DEV_CAP_DESCRIPTOR *)NextCap;
+
+    CapLength = DevCapDesc->Length;
+    if ((CapLength < OFFSET_OF (EFI_USB_DEV_CAP_DESCRIPTOR, CapData)) || (CapLength > Remaining)) {
+      return FALSE;
+    }
+
     if ((DevCapDesc->DescriptorType == USB_DESC_TYPE_DEV_CAP) && (DevCapDesc->DevCapabilityType == USB_DEV_CAP_SUPPERSPEED_USB)) {
-      return TRUE;
+      IsSsDevice = TRUE;
     }
+
+    NextCap   += CapLength;
+    Remaining -= CapLength;
   }
 
-  return FALSE;
+  return IsSsDevice;
 }
 
 /**
